-07-16. Holds notable historical significance, documented across 50 language editions of Wikipedia. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "Established on July 16, 1864, the University of Bucharest is a pivotal institution in Romania, serving as a cornerstone of higher education in Eastern Europe. Founded by the prominent Romanian politician and academic Spiru Haret, it has played an instrumental role in shaping the intellectual landscape of the region. With faculties ranging from history and philosophy to law and economics, the university has contributed to the cultivation of a modern Romanian identity in the wake of national unification and socio-political change following the 1859 union of the principalities of Moldavia and Wallachia.

